sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User Browser
    participant S as Server

    rect rgb(255, 243, 224)
        Note over U,S: Manual fetch() approach -- ~25 lines of JS

        U->>+S: GET /api/provinces
        Note right of S: Express route returns JSON array
        S-->>-U: [{id:1, name:"Bohol"}, ...]

        Note over U: JSON.parse(response)
        Note over U: Loop: document.createElement for each province
        Note over U: Build option/li elements in memory
        Note over U: select.appendChild(fragment)

        Note over U: Must also handle errors, loading spinner, empty state
    end

    rect rgb(232, 245, 233)
        Note over U,S: htmx approach -- 0 lines of JS

        U->>+S: hx-get="/provinces"
        Note right of S: Express route returns HTML partial
        S-->>-U: <option value="1">Bohol</option>...

        Note over U: htmx auto-swaps response into target element
        Note over U: No manual parsing, no loop, no appendChild
    end

    Note over U,S: htmx eliminates boilerplate: no fetch, no JSON.parse, no DOM manipulation
